From 9e52fa7bf92ee9eea61a17de7912d815fa6f452f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:58:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] linkbus: ring seam for the NAOMI M3 comm board (PLAN_V2
 2.10, D-061)

NaomiM3Comm now reaches the ring through linkbus::RingBackend instead of
calling NaomiNetwork directly. With no backend installed it uses the UDP
backend, which wraps naomiNetwork and keeps the 8412d3d8a behaviour: take
with a 100 ms poll, "No data received" log, zero-filled whole-region copy,
transcnt from the predecessor's packet number, send after take, and any
FlycastException zeroing comm_status1/2.

Also added:
- InMemoryHub: star hub for all seats in one process with an equal delay L,
  using the same wire format and checks as remote seats (tests, and the
  reference for the TypeScript hub).
- Mailbox ring backend over a MailboxIo, with a byte-exact buffer reference
  and an Emscripten JS bridge (SharedArrayBuffer mailbox, postMessage hook).
  No transport (no WebRTC).
- Wire checks with edition tag refusal, session tag, slot geometry.
- FramePacer: one local frame per hub tick for each seat (CLAIM_FAIRNESS
  R3), with bounded hold, catch-up and backlog.
- LinkBusHandshake: when the host installed a backend before load, the role
  is known and SetNaomiNetworkConfig() runs synchronously in init().
- Standalone unit tests (tests/linkbus), built with emcc and run under node.

